1️⃣ Consumer Lag (Very Common)
Problem

Consumer is too slow to process messages.

Example:

Producer → 10,000 messages/sec
Consumer → 2,000 messages/sec

Result:

Kafka Consumer Lag increases
Symptoms

High lag in monitoring

Messages delayed

Notification or transaction processing slow

Solution

Increase consumer instances

Increase topic partitions

Optimize message processing

Use batch processing

Example scaling:

Before
1 Consumer → 1 Partition

After
4 Consumers → 4 Partitions
2️⃣ Message Duplication

Kafka guarantees at-least-once delivery, so duplicates may occur.

Example
Consumer processes message
Consumer crashes before committing offset
Kafka re-delivers message
Solution

Implement idempotent consumers

Use unique transaction IDs

Store processed IDs in DB/cache

Example strategy:

transactionId = 12345
If already processed → skip
3️⃣ Offset Commit Issues
Problem

Offsets are committed incorrectly.

Example:

Offset committed before processing

If the service crashes:

Message lost
Solution

Use manual commit after processing.

Example:

@KafkaListener(topics = "transactions")
public void consume(String msg, Acknowledgment ack) {

    processMessage(msg);

    ack.acknowledge();   // commit after processing
}
4️⃣ Broker Down / Cluster Failure

Kafka clusters usually have multiple brokers.

Example failure:

Broker 1 DOWN
Solution

Kafka uses replication.

Example:

Topic Partition
   |
   |-- Leader (Broker 1)
   |-- Replica (Broker 2)
   |-- Replica (Broker 3)

If leader fails:

Replica becomes new leader

No data loss.

